a variable is like a box/jar/container which is used to store something
the value we want to store decides the data type to pick
What are different data types in Java?

nonDecimalNumber -->[Byte/short/int/long]
decimalNumber    -->[float/double]
single character -->[char]
true/false       -->[boolean]

========================day17==================================================

smallest unit to measure memory is bit & 1 byte = 8 bits
If a data type fits in range of multiple data types  Select the one which consumes the least memory

Types of Data Type:
 1. Primitive Data Type [byte,short, int, long, float, double, char, boolean]
    we know in advance how much memory they will consume
    we can use them directly without creating the object

 2. Non- Primitive data Type [String/Array....etc]
    we don't know in advance how much memory they will consume
    we cannot use them directly we need to create the object